==Strategy==
Because Papuu spawns only after base hit and three UltraBaaBaas spawn during the initial wave, you can easily [[cheese]] the stage by stacking massive quantities of units and easily demolish her with the sheer combined damage. While Papuu is Wave Immune, Wave Units can still kill Puffington quickly, leaving her open to attack.

After killing the first two UltraBaaBaas and the rest of the initial spawn wave, you can use [[Rover Cat (Rare Cat)|Catellite]], [[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Eraser Cat]] and/or [[Ancient Egg: N108 (Super Rare Cat)|Soap Cat]] to hold back the third UltraBaaBaa indefinitely.

For the rest of the lineup, Cats with [[Wave Attack]]/[[Surge Attack]]/[[Explosion]] will work extremely well, the most notorious example is [[Talents|Talented]] [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut]]. other attackers such as [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]], and [[Food Stall Cat (Rare Cat)|Cafeteria Cat]] also work really well due to having extreme DPS when stacked up.

A number of Ubers can be stacked using this method, and as long as they neither have [[Barrier Breaker]] nor deal more than 266,000 damage per hit, you can easily stack up to the maximum Cat limit of 50.

When you are ready to unleash the death ball you have created, spawn a Barrier Breaker to kill the UltraBaaBaa and make sure to use [[Ototo Corps|Iron Wall Cannon]] just before hitting the base to prevent Mr. Puffington from killing your stack. You should be able to erase everything that comes on base hit and just have a few peons left.

Also make sure to have ALL anti-starred alien treasures from cats of the cosmos.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Talents|Talented]] [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut]] - His extreme damage through [[Explosion]] will evaporate everything on base hit if you take the time to stack him.
*[[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Slime Cat]] - Can be stacked fast and does a lot of damage, make sure Papuu doesn't kill your stack immediately.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*[[Kalisa (Uber Rare Cat)|Divine Kalisa]] - Works in a similar way to A. Bahamut and can be stacked but needs precise Curse Blast timing to prevent her from dying.
*[[Kasli the Bane (Uber Rare Cat)|Kasli, Daughter of Chaos]] - Can also be stacked and will permanently curse Papuu once hit at least once. Be wary of Mr. Puffington though, as he can easily kill Dasli if she is not properly protected.
*[[Cat Machine (Uber Rare Cat)|Cat Machine]] - Allows for the stack to survive being pushed back as well as buying you time to defend it and does very well into the other aliens. Be aware of both Mr. Puffington and Papuu as it will be cripped by Mr. Puffington's Curse and Papuu's toxic if not properly protected.
*[[Hades the Punisher (Uber Rare Cat)|Hades the Punisher]] - Thanks to his toxic immunity and high health, he can be an incredibly useful unit to tank. This is especially true when stacked.
*[[Netherworld Nymph Lunacia (Uber Rare Cat)|Netherworld Nymph Lunacia]] - She can act as a substitute for A. bahamut if one is unable to get his talents. In addition, some of her immunities are toxic and curse, so she won't have to worry about getting cursed by Mr. Puffington nor intoxicated by Pappu, and she's strong against angels which means by just adding 10 or more Lunacias, Pappu will go down in one go.

==Trivia==
*This stage's Japanese name, Tenshi ni Yami Songu o (天使に闇ソングを, "Dark Song to an Angel"), is a reference to ''Tenshi ni Rabu Songu o'' (天使にラブソングを, "Love Song to an Angel"), the Japanese name of the American musical crime-comedy film ''[[wikipedia:Sister Act|Sister Act]]''.
**Tenshi ni Rabu Songu o is also the Japanese name of ''[[wikipedia:Prison School|Prison School]]''<nowiki>'</nowiki>s [[wikia:prison-school:Chapter 224|224th chapter]], titled Sister Act in English.
*This stage's English name might reference [[wikipedia:Requiem for a Dream|Requiem for a Dream]], a 1978 psychological drama novel that saw a film adaptation released in 2000.

